      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. I think of all this as TODO work (I guess I\u0027m hoping for something better than this for the hidden configs). It seems like there are 3 categories then:\n1) hidden configs\n2) configs we don\u0027t like but might be stuck with: ARCH_HISI, PCIE_KIRIN\n3) stuff that needs to be fixed upstream and backported\n\nbut I still prefer a single TODO list. I guess we can move the !hidden ones to gki_defconfig when we concede we won\u0027t have any fix for them... but maybe the whole thing should be CONFIG_GKI_HACKS_TO_FIX instead of calling it a MODULE_HELPER.\n\nMaybe we\u0027ll also want CONFIG_GKI_HACKS_FOR_HISILICON for ARCH_HISI and PCIE_KIRIN, and generally CONFIG_GKI_HACKS_FOR_\u003cvendor\u003e where we can call out per-vendor config requirements that we want to get rid of someday...\n\nLet\u0027s see what other folks think.",
